WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.369 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:06.372
-Welcome back.
Someone last week wrote,

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.342
"Why are you wearing a sweater?
Are you some kind of hippie?"

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.010
I'd love to see a hippie

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.279
afford one of my sweaters.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.314
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.983
[ Chuckling ]
I don't a-think so.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:19.952
[ Laughs ]

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.454
Disney World reopened,
and we made a joke

00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:24.724
saying it smelled
like wet Goofy.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.892
Some of you think Goofy --
We've gone through this before.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.561
Some of you think
Goofy is a cow, not a dog.

00:00:29.561 --> 00:00:34.334
A solution offered by one of you
was to say "wet Pluto."

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:38.671
If you think it's more fun
wet Pluto than wet Goofy,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.005
be my guest.

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.674
Me?

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.877
I want the jokes to land.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.047
Guys, I've been saying
"House of Dragon."

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.883
It's "House of the Dragon."

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.251
I am finally caught up.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.722
I will agree, I think
it's getting really good.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.658
I will admit, for the first few
episodes, I was calling it

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.060
"House of Dragging."

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.063
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.668
Sometimes the dialogue
is a little...

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.303
on the nose.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:15.074
Like last week when Daemon said,
"I can't have sex with you.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.076
I'm your uncle,"
and Rhaenyra said,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:20.246
"No, no, I incest."

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.082
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.786
I just don't think

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.822
people talked like that
back then.

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.228
Hey, we implied that Sherlock
Holmes was addicted to opium.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.197
He was addicted to cocaine,

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.733
which was covered
in my favorite

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.236
of Sir Arthur
Conan Doyle's book,

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.972
"Sherlock Holmes
and the 400-Page Screenplay."

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.774
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.642 --> 00:01:53.346
[British accent] "It's
an unsuitable script, Holmes!"

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.782
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.284
[Normal voice]
But you know what?

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.418
He may have done cocaine --

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.921
He got the job done.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.457
He solved the cases.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.459
That's why it's fine. He's o--

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:11.463
He's A-OK with me, buddy.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:14.734
Sherlock is to me what
Herschel Walker is to the GOP.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.436
I don't care!

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.606
We showed a Little League
baseball card

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.009
of Mark Zuckerberg from 1974.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.677
He was not alive till then.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.812
It wasn't until 1984

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:29.616
that he was pulled
from his milk bath.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.584
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.756
I was told that peanuts, cashews
and almonds are not nuts.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.624
They are legumes, seeds.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.227
Some even said they're drupes,
whatever drupes are.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.395
And let me just tell you,
if peanuts, cashews,

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.632
and almonds are not nuts,

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:49.135
there's no such [bleep] thing
as a nut.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.803
Okay?

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.738
If the best three nuts
aren't nuts,

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:56.075
I'm [bleep] out on nuts.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.012
If they're out, I'm out.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.880
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.151
Hey, we did a th--
We were...

00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:08.754
Donald Trump said
Democrats cheat like dogs,

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.424
and we were surprised because
who thinks dogs cheat?

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.527
And quite a few of you said
that maybe he thought that

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:20.700
because of this famous photo
where that dog is obviously...

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:27.307
So, I guess I want to apologize
to Donald Trump.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.909
He obviously thinks
that dogs cheat

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.045
because he saw this painting

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.213
and thought it was a photo.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.182
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.658
Oh, we were talking about --
arguing that Fred

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:48.227
from Scooby Doo
was a straight white man.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:49.629
We said he definitely was

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.798
because he was a white guy
with a van.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.467
One of the jackals said
that it was Daphne's van.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:56.803
I dug into it online.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:04:00.806
Everybody seems to agree
that it's Fred's van.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.741
We could always
just agree to disagree,

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:06.211
as long as we agree
that this van right here

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:09.048
definitely belongs to this guy.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.551
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.887
Hashtag not an ad.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.923
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.030
Oh, we talked about
"Six Million Dollar Man"

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.631
and we joked --
I joked and came up with

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.132
what its title
would have been in France.

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:31.137
It turned out "Six Million
Dollar Man" was on in France,

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:34.807
and it was "L'homme qui valait
trois milliards."

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.475
You think I'm joking?
I'm not joking.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:37.576
Alex, roll the clip.

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:38.911 line:0%
[ Theme music plays ]

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.947 line:0%
-[ Speaking French ]

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.787
-So, you're wondering
why is it...

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:50.556
So, "trois milliards"
is "3 billion."

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:54.827
So "The Six Million Dollar Man"
in France was the --

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:58.097
was "the 3 billion franc man."

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.498
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.134
And if you're wondering,
was 3 billion francs

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:05.304
equal to $6 million
at the time, it wasn't.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.573
That was worth upwards
of $70 million,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.575
which means that the French --

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.810
I guess the French producers
who put it on TV were like,

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.645
[French accent] "Eh, you cannot
build a robot man

00:05:13.645 --> 00:05:14.914
for 6 million."

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.082
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:20.153
"No one will believe it."

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.320
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.354
[Normal voice]
'Cause they're --

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:24.423
just 'cause of unions
over there.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.158
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:27.827
The problem with the show,
it didn't work

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:32.665
because it was -- the title
was tied to the exchange rate.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.833
So...

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.436
So, like one week, you know,
it would be

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.538
"qui valait trois milliards,
" and then the next week,

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:42.908
it would be
"deux point cinq milliards,"

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:44.409
"trois point un."

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:45.744
And people were like,

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.747
"Is it the same show?
Am I...?"

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.081
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:50.283
Didn't work.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:57.122
We made a joke about there being
police tape on a bathroom door,

00:05:57.122 --> 00:06:00.626
and Graphics did me dirty.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.394
That's -- first of all,
it's a stall door,

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.863
not a bathroom door.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.532
And also -- so, the way
police tape works is

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.035
it's supposed to make it harder
to get into something.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.737
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.606
Whereas this, you would
just open the door

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:16.275
like any other time.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:19.345
And so, of course, I went down
to their weird little cave

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.846
and I was like,
"Hey, Graphics."

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:22.180
And they were like, "Whaaat?"

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.349
And I was like,

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.485
"Do you not realize
that if it was like this,

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:28.588
you could just open the door
to someone's bathroom stall?"

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.591
And they said, "Maybe that's
what we want you to do."

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.493
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:41.533
We discussed the uproar
about Black hobbits

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:43.035
in the new "Lord of the Rings."

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:45.037
And a fan very passionately
wrote me

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.373
and said, "You know,
this wasn't even a story.

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.041
People were not upset
about Black hobbits.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.943
This was created by the press
to draw attention to the show."

00:06:51.943 --> 00:06:53.779
And I thought, you know what?
That does make sense.

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:57.082
Sometimes articles, you know,
they basically pick

00:06:57.082 --> 00:06:59.285
one or two tweets
from people with no followers

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:01.587
and they try to create
an uproar out of that.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.589
And so I --
you know, in my head,

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.424
I was feeling apologetic
toward the fact

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.858
that we even
drew attention to it.

00:07:06.858 --> 00:07:08.995
And then this very same person
went on and continued,

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.129
"We're not upset about that.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.797
We're upset
about the Black elves."

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.133
And I was just like [bleep] off.
What am I even doing?

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.768
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:21.674
We asked our international
viewers to send in postcards.

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:24.509 line:0%
We'll put our address here
once again.

00:07:24.509 --> 00:07:26.846 line:0%
Or not. I don't know.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.814 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:30.315 line:0%
And we have a P.O. box,

00:07:30.315 --> 00:07:31.784 line:0%
and we're gonna take
all the postcards

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.486 line:0%
from the international jackals,
and then we'll do a drawing.

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:36.955 line:0%
And then I'm gonna take
a little bit of my sweater money

00:07:36.955 --> 00:07:38.858
and pay to ship you.

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:40.192
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:42.495
And so we didn't think in a week
that we'd get

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.497
international postcards,
which of course, we didn't.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.131
We got some real jerks
from the States

00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:47.332
who already are sending them.

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:49.502
And first of all, I said,

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.070
you have to write --
in order to enter,

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.772
you have to write,
"I am a jackal

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.640
and I don't deserve
your kindness."

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.743
And then this man or woman
just wrote,

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.379
"Seth is a jackass,"

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.981
and then gave their name
as Bobby Corrections,

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:04.650
which I don't think...

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.185
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:11.223
Or maybe that's me.
Maybe they think I'm Bobby.

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:12.658
Yeah, they sent it to me.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.995
Anyway, but I did like that
it's a correctional facility.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.797
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:25.204
Uh, Finland is not Scandinavian.

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:28.240
Based on how snooty the Danes,
Swedes, and Norwegians were

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.876
about the error, I'd say, uh,

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:31.877
I think that's
for the best, Finland.

00:08:31.877 --> 00:08:33.279
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.881 --> 00:08:39.185
Oh, so, we mentioned
last week as well,

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.720
my beloved Steelers
played the Jets

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.154
last weekend in Pittsburgh.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.623
And I mentioned that one of our
crew members, Kenny Coyle,

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:47.527
proposed a bet
leading up to that week

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.161
where he said
that if the Jets won,

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:50.629
I would have to
mention it on air,

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:52.097
and if the Steelers won,

00:08:52.097 --> 00:08:54.933
he would wear a Steelers
half-shirt to work,

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:57.068
like a crop-top jersey,
I guess.

00:08:57.068 --> 00:08:59.237
And we talked at the time,
we were a little surprised

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:01.907
'cause that did not seem
like a very equitable bet.

00:09:01.907 --> 00:09:04.410
It seemed like Kenny did
not mind about that part of it,

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.345
that maybe...

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:09.481
maybe Kenny was angling for
one of the outcomes there.

00:09:09.481 --> 00:09:12.451
Anyway, but then the Jets win,

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:14.720
and I come in on Monday morning,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.221
and Kenny is all smiles

00:09:16.221 --> 00:09:18.657
and he's wearing
a Jets crop top.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.893
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:25.765
It turns out the crop top
was not a punishment at all.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.468
Wore it Monday, wore it Tuesday,
wore it...

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:30.969
And finally today
I had to say, "Kenny,

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:34.973
you've got to stop wearing
a crop top to work."

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:37.043
And he was like, "Why?"
And I was like,

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:39.078
"Well, it could be an HR issue."

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:42.414
And then Kenny
very confidently said,

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:45.251
"HR can't touch it
if it's a bet."

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:47.586
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.154
I'm like, "What are you
talking about?"

00:09:49.154 --> 00:09:51.123
He goes, he goes,
"If it's a bet,

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.158
it's outside of their purview."

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:55.328
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.035
I did, after the game --

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.770
to show I was a good sport

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.906
about the fact that the Jets
beat the Steelers,

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:13.145
I took a photo with former Jet
wide receiver Santonio Holmes.

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:16.682
There he is, and there's
the Super Bowl ring he won

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:18.517
when he was with the Jets.

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.387
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.723
What's that?

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:26.358
It's not?

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:28.694
How are you so sure?

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:31.530
Oh, 'cause he wasn't
alive in 1969?

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.232
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:35.234
Yeah.

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:36.268
Well, I didn't know --
Oh!

00:10:37.569 --> 00:10:39.205
I'm tr-- I'm...

00:10:40.172 --> 00:10:42.174
I'm trying to be a good sport.

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:43.509
I didn't know.

00:10:43.509 --> 00:10:45.711
[ Laughter ]

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:48.214
It's not my fault
it's been that long!

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:50.049
[ Laughter ]

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:57.189
Um...

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.958
I also said that

00:10:59.958 --> 00:11:01.794
the Jets being 2-2
is like their Super Bowl

00:11:01.794 --> 00:11:03.662
and that it was really hard
getting to work

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:07.299
'cause Fifth Avenue was
all backed up from the parade.

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:08.801
And somebody wrote,

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:10.636
"Ticker-tape parades
are historically done

00:11:10.636 --> 00:11:13.072
on lower Broadway, between
Battery Park and City Hall.

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:14.707
They do not happen
on Fifth Avenue."

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.743
What makes you think
that if the Jets had won,

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:19.578
they wouldn't [bleep] it up?

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:21.447
[ Laughter ]

00:11:25.584 --> 00:11:27.086
Wouldn't be, like, a weird float

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:28.487
halfway on
a Staten Island ferry?

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:30.022
They're like,
"What the [bleep] happened?!"

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:32.391
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.661 --> 00:11:39.131
We had a very
sport-themed week...

00:11:41.099 --> 00:11:44.169
...because we also -- you know,
obviously, we're very invested

00:11:44.169 --> 00:11:45.570
in the New York Mets
on this show

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:49.074
because the entire staff
is Mets fans,

00:11:49.074 --> 00:11:51.076
excluding Wally.

00:11:51.076 --> 00:11:53.845
Cue Card Wally is a Yankees fan.

00:11:53.845 --> 00:11:56.715
But mostly we're Mets fans,
and there was a Closer Look

00:11:56.715 --> 00:11:58.249
where we made fun of the fact
that the Mets,

00:11:58.249 --> 00:12:00.586
despite winning 101 games,
did not win their division

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:03.855
and now have a tough path
to the World Series.

00:12:03.855 --> 00:12:06.792
And so, I get in the --
I get in the elevator

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:09.295
with, you know, Jim and John,
the security guys,

00:12:09.295 --> 00:12:11.263
Mets fans, and they were like,
"What's with

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:12.764
all the Mets burns?"
And I was like,

00:12:12.764 --> 00:12:14.199
"Hey, Sal wrote it.

00:12:14.199 --> 00:12:16.068
You know,
Sal put the Mets burns in.

00:12:16.068 --> 00:12:18.336
He's a self-hating Mets fan.
He did it all."

00:12:18.336 --> 00:12:20.072
And then one of them said,
"I was worried

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:22.374
that Wally
would change the cards

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:26.711
to make all the jokes about how
Aaron Judge hit 62 home runs."

00:12:26.711 --> 00:12:28.147
And then
the other security guard

00:12:28.147 --> 00:12:29.781
said if Wally changed the cards,

00:12:29.781 --> 00:12:31.950
he would have made it
about Wally.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.853
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:36.588 --> 00:12:38.256
Jim and John,

00:12:38.256 --> 00:12:40.259
the Statler and Waldorf...

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:43.195
[ Laughter ]

00:12:43.195 --> 00:12:45.964
They both just went like,
"Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:12:45.964 --> 00:12:47.633
"Ah-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!"

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.368
[ Laughter ]

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.805
Hey, you know,
we don't ever have...

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:54.706
We don't ever let
audience members

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:56.708
in to the studio
for "Corrections,"

00:12:56.708 --> 00:12:57.877
but we have a very special one.

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.177
I mentioned him
on the show tonight.

00:12:59.177 --> 00:13:01.446
Matt Parker is here.

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:04.916
Matt Parker was -- sent me
the first YouTube video

00:13:04.916 --> 00:13:06.819
when I was doing
the attic shows,

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:10.055
basically commenting
on how I could improve

00:13:10.055 --> 00:13:12.057
things like the lighting
and the sound.

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:15.327
In a way, Matt is
the original jackal.

00:13:15.327 --> 00:13:17.062
And in a way, he's responsible

00:13:17.062 --> 00:13:20.566
for this death spiral
I've been in ever since.

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:13:22.234 --> 00:13:24.335
But he was a really important
part of the show

00:13:24.335 --> 00:13:25.838
during the pandemic, so I'm
really happy he's here.

00:13:25.838 --> 00:13:27.006
Thanks for being here, Matt.

00:13:27.006 --> 00:13:28.306
Is Matt there? Where is he?
There is Matt.

00:13:28.306 --> 00:13:29.474
Thank you for being here.

00:13:29.474 --> 00:13:33.611
And that, I think,
is all we have, you guys.

00:13:33.611 --> 00:13:36.749
Why don't you see me
next week?

